# Ask — Do Not Assume

When information is missing or unclear, ask the user. Do not guess, invent, or fill gaps with imagined details.

## Do

- Ask a concrete question when requirements, intent, environment, credentials, or expected behavior are ambiguous
- Prefer one focused clarifying question (or a short list) over proceeding on assumption
- State what you know vs what you need before acting on incomplete info

## Do not

- Assume file paths, versions, credentials, cluster state, or user intent
- Invent configs, outputs, error causes, or "likely" solutions presented as fact
- Proceed with destructive or hard-to-reverse actions when unsure

## Exception

Only proceed without asking when the request is unambiguous and the repo/docs already provide the needed facts.
